l": 481.0, "s12m_bear": 324.72, "s12m_base": 453.64, "s12m_bull": 552.88, "s36m_bear": 252.07, "s36m_base": 519.37, "s36m_bull": 684.88}], "briefing": [{"kind": "takeaway", "title": "Today in one sentence", "text": "The market ended the week near its best level of the year, while a few companies on our list are still well below their highs."}, {"kind": "alert", "title": "AMD caught up with the experts", "text": "AMD went up about 183% in one year. It now trades at $608, almost exactly what experts expected it to be worth a year from now ($608). When a stock reaches its target early, it needs new good news to keep climbing."}, {"kind": "alert", "title": "Borrowing got more expensive", "text": "The U.S. government now pays about 5.0% a year to borrow for 10 years, up from about 4.1% a year ago. When safe bonds pay more, some investors move money out of pricey tech stocks."}, {"kind": "alert", "title": "Healthcare had a good Friday", "text": "Healthcare companies rose about 2.1% on Friday while tech slipped 0.6%. One day is not a trend; we will see if it repeats."}, {"kind": "lesson", "title": "Lesson 1: What is beta?", "text": "Beta tells you how much a stock moves compared with the whole market. A beta of 1 moves like the market. A beta of 2 tends to move twice as much, up and down. NVIDIA has a beta of about 2.2 and Rocket Lab about 2.6, so they are roller coasters. Eli Lilly is about 0.45, a much calmer ride."}, {"kind": "coverage", "title": "About the data", "text": "Expert price targets are available for NVDA, TSM, AMD, GOOGL, AMZN, MSFT, META, LMT and GE. For the others we only use price movements."}], "news": [{"date": "2026-10-09", "tickers": ["ALL", "LLY", "ISRG", "MSFT", "NVDA"], "effect": "watch", "title": "Health stocks up, tech stocks down on Friday", "summary": "On the last trading day of the week, healthcare companies on the Nasdaq rose about 2.1% on average, while technology companies slipped about 0.6%.", "why": "When money moves from one group of stocks to another, people call it a rotation. One day is not a trend, but if it keeps happening, our tech-heavy companies could lag while health companies like Eli Lilly do better.", "source": "Financial Modeling Prep sector data", "url": ""}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "tickers": ["TSM", "NVDA", "AMD", "AVGO"], "effect": "good", "title": "TSMC's sales jumped 55% in a year", "summary": "TSMC, the factory that builds chips for NVIDIA, AMD and Apple, reported September sales of about NT$512 billion, 54.6% more than a year earlier. Sales for the first nine months of 2026 grew about 41%.", "why": "TSMC builds the chips that power AI. When its sales keep growing this fast, it means companies are still buying lots of AI chips, which is good news for the AI suppliers on our list.", "source": "TSMC press release", "url": "https://pr.tsmc.com/english/news/3343"}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "tickers": ["ALL", "NVDA", "AMD", "META", "AMZN"], "effect": "bad", "title": "The Fed may raise interest rates again", "summary": "Notes from the Federal Reserve's last meeting showed most officials expect another rate increase this year, because prices are still rising about 3.4% a year, well above their 2% goal. The Fed already raised rates in September.", "why": "Higher interest rates make borrowing more expensive and make safe savings pay more. That can pull money away from stocks, especially fast-growing companies that look expensive, like many AI stocks.", "source": "Associated Press via News4JAX", "url": "https://www.news4jax.com/business/2026/10/07/federal-reserve-officials-expect-another-rate-hike-will-be-needed-this-year-according-to-minutes/"}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "tickers": ["ALL"], "effect": "watch", "title": "Coming up: the Fed decides on rates Oct. 28-29", "summary": "The Federal Reserve's next meeting is October 28-29. According to the same report, traders expect the Fed to wait at that meeting and raise rates in December.", "why": "Fed meeting days often make the whole market jumpy. A surprise in either direction can move every stock on our list.", "source": "Associated Press via News4JAX", "url": "https://www.news4jax.com/business/2026/10/07/federal-reserve-officials-expect-another-rate-hike-will-be-needed-this-year-according-to-minutes/"}, {"date": "2026-08-10", "tickers": ["RKLB"], "effect": "bad", "title": "Rocket Lab's big new rocket might slip to 2027", "summary": "Rocket Lab said the window to launch its larger Neutron rocket before the end of 2026 is narrowing, and a filing said the first flight could slip into 2027. A fuel tank broke during a test in January, which already caused a delay.", "why": "Investors are paying today for rockets Rocket Lab plans to fly tomorrow. Delays push back the money those launches would earn, which is one reason the stock is far below its high.", "source": "Spaceflight Now", "url": "https://spaceflightnow.com/2026/08/10/window-for-2026-launch-debut-of-rocket-labs-neutron-rocket-is-narrowing-as-development-continues/"}], "treasury10y": [{"month": "2025-10", "yield_pct": 4.06}, {"month": "2025-11", "yield_pct": 4.09}, {"month": "2025-12", "yield_pct": 4.14}, {"month": "2026-01", "yield_pct": 4.21}, {"month": "2026-02", "yield_pct": 4.13}, {"month": "2026-03", "yield_pct": 4.25}, {"month": "2026-04", "yield_pct": 4.32}, {"month": "2026-05", "yield_pct": 4.48}, {"month": "2026-06", "yield_pct": 4.47}, {"month": "2026-07", "yield_pct": 4.6}, {"month": "2026-08", "yield_pct": 4.68}, {"month": "2026-09", "yield_pct": 4.99}]}